        "id": 1312815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-28T19:30:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027d be good to discuss this addition in an API owners call. Was it discussed in the one that I missed this week?\nI\u0027m curious regarding the motivation here. It seems like we\u0027d be increasing the burden on WG proposals in ways that may discourage folks from getting proposals adopted. It might make sense (to me) to apply this regardless of WG adoption. Anyway, I think it\u0027s worthwhile to chat through this in a high bandwidth env.",
      "revId": "0f6dd219ce1704b7a2a4fe5978edbd64cacdff2a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a40b1ce9_0b4b39b8",
        "filename": "site/blink/launching-features/index.md",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 415,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-28T22:03:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 on the API owners discussing this at a meeting. This change comes from some discussions around some CSS and Editing features that were proposed to ship or shipped in various browsers without the relevant WG having a chance to weigh in on the final state. I\u0027m thinking of a feature\u0027s WG as having an analogous position to the TAG or other vendors, in that they have some expertise in the area that we should pay attention to, but of course they don\u0027t get to just veto shipping. It\u0027s hard to apply this regardless of WG adoption because not all features have a natural WG to present them to, and it doesn\u0027t feel right to say that we have to present a feature to a WG that said it didn\u0027t want to talk about it.\n\nYou\u0027re right that this could decrease people\u0027s motivation to get features adopted, but I think the overall loss of unilateral control over the feature is a much bigger reason to avoid adoption, and we have to rely on the organization\u0027s commitment to Do The Right Thing in both cases.",
      "parentUuid": "1ec6beeb_b37a5122",
      "revId": "0f6dd219ce1704b7a2a4fe5978edbd64cacdff2a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
